1. Population Structure Analysis
# Population stratification was assessed using linkage disequilibrium (LD)-pruned variants followed by Principal Component Analysis (PCA).

1.1 LD Pruning
# LD pruning was performed to obtain a subset of approximately independent variants suitable for ancestry inference.
plink \
  --bfile input_prefix \
  --indep-pairwise 250 50 0.9 \
  --out output_prefix

# Description of Parameters
--bfile                         Prefix of PLINK binary genotype files.
--indep-pairwise 250 50 0.9	    Performs LD pruning using a 250-variant window, shifting by 50 variants, with an r2 threshold of 0.9.
--out	                          Prefix for output files.

# Main Output Files
output_prefix.prune.in
output_prefix.prune.out

1.2 Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
# Principal component analysis was performed using the LD-pruned variants in order to infer population structure and generate ancestry covariates.
plink \
  --bfile pruned_input_prefix \
  --pca 10 header tabs \
  --out output_prefix

# Description of Parameters
--pca 10    Computes the first 10 principal components.
header	    Adds column names to the output file.
tabs	      Produces tab-delimited output files.

# Main Output File
output_prefix.eigenvec

# The resulting principal components (PC1-PC10) were subsequently included as covariates in downstream association analyses.

