#Notes

All analyses were performed using PLINK binary genotype files.
Principal components were included as covariates to account for population stratification.
REGENIE Step 1 LOCO predictions were incorporated into all Step 2 association analyses.
Common variant analyses were conducted under additive, dominant, and recessive inheritance models using logistic regression for binary traits and linear regression for quantitative traits.
Rare variant analyses were performed using gene-based aggregation tests.
High- and moderate-impact variants were analyzed using the GENE_P framework.
Low-impact and modifier variants were analyzed using the SKAT-O method.
Binary trait analyses used SPA correction for common variants and Firth correction for rare variant analyses to account for case–control imbalance and sparse data.
Quantitative trait analyses excluding treated individuals were performed to minimize treatment-related confounding.
Multiple testing correction across inheritance models was performed using Bonferroni adjustment.
